\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces The maintenance chain. Tag marks (CaMKII Thr286), proteins build (CREB/BDNF/actin), myelin wraps (up to 100$\times $), replay writes (10--20$\times $ compressed), ledger checks ($\geq $95\% coverage). Each station is defined on first use and graded in text.}}{16}{figure.2.1}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces The ratchet across deaths. The maintenance chain from Figure~\ref {fig:maintenance-chain} becomes, at population scale, teaching $\to $ external marks $\to $ repeated practice $\to $ replay in conversation $\to $ checkable library. Each death is a turnover event like protein turnover; the ledger holds the pattern.}}{23}{figure.3.1}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces The slow vault. Fast entries add $E_t$, two doors drain it via $R_t$ and $Q_t$, the stock $S_t$ feeds back as $S_{t-1}$. When $Q_t$ sleeps, $S_t$ compounds where no one is looking.}}{30}{figure.4.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Two Day-1 machines and one Day-N mirror. ABS issuance and dividend recap volume both running hot into 2025, then one bank's \$100.4B return to book when the QSPE permission slip died. Same loan from slow memory, taken many times, partly returned when one gate closed.}}{31}{figure.4.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Day-1 vs Day-N mirror timeline. Left: Day-1 monetization (ABS \$388.1B at +43.3\% YoY, recaps \$81B) pays fees now while $S_t$ rises off book ($Q_t \approx 0$). Right: Day-N mirror (BofA Jan 1 2010: +\$100.4B assets, +\$106.7B liabilities, \$6.2B equity charge) forces $S_t$ back on book when QSPE dies. Dashed wall is discrete: $\psi $ jumps $0 \to 1$ in one period. Sources: \texttt {sifma\_abs\_2024\_v1.json}, \texttt {divrecap\_market\_v1.json}, BofA 10-K acc. 0000950123-11-018743, \texttt {edgar\_K\_panel\_v1.json}.}}{36}{figure.4.3}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Pod hierarchy with $K$ labels. Platform allocates \$100--\$200M per pod (\$79B, 320+ teams, \texttt {pods\_goodhart\_v1.json}) with $K$ at pod $A$ only under no cross-margin. Breakers ($-$5\% halve, $-$7.5\% terminate, Millennium automatic; Citadel negotiated; 15--20\% turnover as feature) bound idiosyncratic loss. Dashed red is the shared factor that bypasses $K$ labels: 50 pods at \$20M gross with $\beta \approx 1$ lose \$40M together at $-5$\% factor when $\rho \to 0.8$ despite $K_A, K_B, K_C$ walls holding individually. Instances: Klavdianos \$100M (Bloomberg Dec 12--13 2023, liquidation Sep--Dec, \texttt {pods\_single\_pod\_autopsies\_v1.json}), Aug 2024 six-pod cluster (Fitzgibbon/Ying/Corones/Murayama/Motegi/Cox) after Nikkei $-12.4$\% and USD/JPY $161 \to 142$.}}{39}{figure.5.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces $K$ evolution 2010 to 2020 after the QSPE was killed. Conduit footprints shrink or persist, never rebuild. The boundary repair sticks.}}{42}{figure.5.2}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Claims funnel: $H$ gated by $\psi $ then capped by $K$. Four $0.7$ gates leave $24\%$ before the cap. When $K$ binds, gating reform cannot raise $P$. Formal identities, not estimates.}}{47}{figure.6.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Gate-latency bars by class: median filing-to-termination from \texttt {recap\_coded298\_v1.json} ($298$ dockets). Unsecured is fastest at $7.3$y, priority and secured longest at $11.6$y. Delay is a gate for those who cannot fund the wait. Activity latency, not adjudicated $\phi $, but economically material.}}{49}{figure.6.2}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces Wall timeline $2006\to 2010\to 2020$ with overlays: BIS credit-to-GDP gap $+11.6\to -9.4$ (blue, stock proxy, left peak to trough, $\approx 21$ pts), charge-offs $0.98\to 3.02\%$ (red dashed, flow, triples after gap peaks), and provision flow $233.6$B at $2009$Q4 vs $40.7$B $2026$Q2 ($5.74\times $, purple bars). Orange shading is the wall $2008$--$2010$ where $S_t$ is forced. Gray arrow is DSR $18.5\to 14.1$ masking stock as flow falls on rates while gap collapses. Sources: \texttt {finance\_falsify\_v1.json, fdic\_coverage\_v1.json, ffiec\_provisions\_wall\_v1.json, bis\_DSR\_US\_v1.json}. Formal $S_t$ law, measured proxies agree.}}{58}{figure.7.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.2}{\ignorespaces Stock versus flow: BIS gap $+11.6\to -9.4$ stores $S_t$, DSR $18.5\to 14.1$ masks it as rates fall, then $Q_t$ spikes $0.98\to 3.02\%$ and provisions jump $5.7\times $ at the wall. Formal stock, measured flow mask.}}{60}{figure.7.2}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.1}{\ignorespaces Apex-offshore hierarchy with $g_4$ gate. Offshore apex holds title ($A\approx 0\Rightarrow K=0$) and controls onshore HoldCo through a treaty/title gate $g_4\to 0$. Operating $H$ sits in OpCo/PropCo while economics stream upstream as fees and dividends. Domestic creditors face $\phi =P/H$ bounded by thin $K$ and $\psi \to 0$ through $g_4$; the domestic observer's $\gamma \to 0$ by design. Moving the apex where attachment fails zeroes $\phi $ before any courthouse gate is debated.}}{66}{figure.8.1}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9.1}{\ignorespaces Parliament competition with NE/DA gain arrows. Six specialists bid via salience $\times $ utility; winner is broadcast in $\sim $200~ms. NE is the volume knob (high gain = tunnel vision, amplifies the current winner); DA is the stake dial (weights planning and affect bids). Different gains = different mind on the same hardware. The threshold $\theta _m$ of the next section is this vote made biophysical.}}{75}{figure.9.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9.2}{\ignorespaces The 60-second loop: gullibility to container to ledger. One minute per loop. Barzakh as fence (gullibility opens it deliberately), muraqaba as watcher (container damps), khayal as rehearsal (ledger writes the next variant). Ledger content makes the witness checkable.}}{79}{figure.9.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9.3}{\ignorespaces TikTok / Reels as co-training: viewer and feed learn at two speeds each. Viewer tags salience via affect (fast hippocampal tag $\to $ slow cortical + myelin, up to 100x), feed tags attention via linger/replay/like (fast session $\to $ slow profile). Cross-coupled, variable-reward, infinite-scroll clips remove the veto slot, so salience gates everything and comparison shifts from 50 peers to the top 0.001\% filtered mock signal. Map becomes territory. Fix is witness at transaction layer + damping by schedule, not willpower.}}{81}{figure.9.3}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10.1}{\ignorespaces The harness loop. Each stage has a distinct job; removing any one reintroduces a measured failure mode (repetition, compounding, hallucination, unverifiability, decoration).}}{88}{figure.10.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10.2}{\ignorespaces The collapse loop. Replacement concentrates the pool, silent collapse keeps loss flat while diversity falls, the fragility spectrum records how far it can fall, and provenance is the only brake that keeps replacement from becoming the default.}}{91}{figure.10.2}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11.1}{\ignorespaces Convergence fan: five independent derivations arrive at one five-organ structure. Independence is load-bearing; if any one road were wrong the others would still arrive.}}{100}{figure.11.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11.2}{\ignorespaces One warp, five arrivals. Different substrates, different methods, same five-organ cycle. Lose one and the gap shows up as a predictable failure mode.}}{100}{figure.11.2}%
